# libddb symbol manifest: every function libddb exports whose name starts with DDB.
#
# Format: one symbol name per line, sorted in byte order (LC_ALL=C sort), no duplicates. Lines
# starting with '#' are comments.
#
# This file is the only copy of the list. DDBGetCapabilities() returns it ("symbols", embedded by
# src/CMakeLists.txt) and every release publishes it next to ddb.h. There is no ABI version in
# it: the ABI is the MAJOR and MINOR of the library version (package.json, ddb_version.h).
# scripts/check-abi.py (CI) fails when the library exports a different list, when an export is
# removed since the previous release without a MAJOR bump of package.json, and when one is
# added without a MINOR (or MAJOR) bump.
# Adding an export: declare it in ddb.h, list it here, bump the MINOR of package.json once per
# release.
#
